---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar';
---

<Layout>
    <Navbar client:load />

    <main class="min-h-screen flex flex-col items-center pt-24 md:pt-32 p-4 md:p-8">
        <div class="max-w-3xl w-full space-y-16 pb-24">
            <!-- Header -->
            <header class="space-y-6 text-center md:text-left">
                <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-surface-paper border border-border-default shadow-sm text-sm font-medium text-text-secondary">
                    <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-brand-primary"></span>
                    The Philosophy
                </div>
                <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tight text-text-primary leading-tight">
                    The End of <br/>
                    <span class="text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-600 via-indigo-600 to-blue-600">"Works on My Machine"</span>
                </h1>
                <p class="text-xl text-text-secondary leading-relaxed font-light max-w-2xl">
                    We are facing a crisis of configuration. The tools we use to build software have become more complex than the software itself. It is time to declare bankruptcy on entropy.
                </p>
            </header>

            <!-- Manifesto Body -->
            <article class="prose prose-lg prose-slate dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
                <div class="space-y-12">
                    
                    <!-- Section 1 -->
                    <section class="space-y-4">
                        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-text-primary">1. Configuration as a First-Class Citizen</h2>
                        <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                            A development environment is not a collection of side effects. It is a software product. It should be versioned, tested, and deployed with the same rigor as your production application. 
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                            Konductor rejects the notion of "setup instructions." If it requires a human to copy-paste commands from a README, it is already broken. We define the environment mathematically using Nix.
                        </p>
                    </section>

                    <!-- Section 2 -->
                    <section class="space-y-4">
                        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-text-primary">2. Hermetic Sovereignty</h2>
                        <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                            True reproducibility requires isolation. Your project should not depend on the version of Python installed on your host OS, nor should it break when you upgrade your laptop.
                        </p>
                        <div class="p-6 bg-surface-paper border border-border-default rounded-xl shadow-sm my-6">
                            <blockquote class="not-italic text-lg font-medium text-text-primary border-l-4 border-brand-accent pl-4">
                                "We build systems that survive the collapse of the internet. If the registry goes down, your team keeps coding."
                            </blockquote>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                            By pinning every dependency—from the compiler down to the libc—we ensure that a build today yields the exact same binary ten years from now.
                        </p>
                    </section>

                    <!-- Section 3 -->
                    <section class="space-y-4">
                        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-text-primary">3. The Polyglot Reality</h2>
                        <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                            Modern systems are not written in a single language. A "Python Project" often involves Rust extensions, Go sidecars, and Node.js frontends. 
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                            Konductor provides a unified substrate. We don't just give you Python; we give you the exact intersection of Python, Rust, and Go required to build your specific system, harmonized in a single shell.
                        </p>
                    </section>
                    
                    <hr class="border-border-subtle" />

                    <!-- Call to Action -->
                    <section class="space-y-6">
                        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary">The Choice is Yours</h2>
                        <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                            You can continue to lease your productivity from vendors who profit from your lock-in. Or you can own your stack.
                        </p>
                        <div class="flex gap-4 pt-4">
                             <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 text-base font-medium text-text-inverse bg-brand-primary rounded-lg hover:bg-brand-primary/90 transition-colors shadow-lg shadow-brand-primary/20">
                                Join the Resistance
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </section>

                </div>
            </article>
        </div>
    </main>
</Layout>
